{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said to him: Go, descend.</b> And if you ask: three warnings, why? Rather, it refers to what He said earlier, 'lest they break through to see,' meaning they cannot ascend, since they are forewarned and stand as written earlier, 'take heed not to go up in the mountain,' and they control their feet. But regarding what you said, 'lest they break through to see' — they do not control their eyes, and they would have an opening to say: our desire is to see our King. He said to him: you spoke well — <b>go, descend</b>, etc. — meaning, I do not punish them except for the ascent; this is what is written: 'they shall not break through to ascend.'" "<b>And Aharon with you.</b> Within the boundary itself, for you are about to explain to them 'let not the priests break through' and so on. Another interpretation <b>go, descend</b> — lest the priests and the people say: Aharon is included in all the warnings like the rest of the people; now when they see you and Aharon ascending, they will say it is permitted to ascend the mountain. Therefore descend and say to them that permission was given only to you and to Aharon."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:55.538439257Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}